{"abstract":[{"text":"Restrict what raw HTML, links and images in a document may do when the Markdown does not come from you.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/RenderingUntrustedMarkdown"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"MarkdownKit"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Rendering Untrusted Markdown"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Markdown can contain raw HTML, links with arbitrary URL schemes, and images that point to local files or to web servers. If the text comes from other users, from a language model, or from a downloaded file, you have to decide what the output may do. MarkdownKit offers restrictions at three levels, from the generators that create HTML to the system component that renders it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Choose-safe-mode-for-HTML","level":3,"text":"Choose safe mode for HTML","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/HtmlGenerator","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" always escapes ","type":"text"},{"code":"href","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"src","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"title","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"alt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and autolink text, so a crafted link or image cannot break out of an attribute. With ","type":"text"},{"code":"HtmlGenerator(safeMode: true)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", it also omits raw HTML and empties URLs with schemes other than ","type":"text"},{"code":"http","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"https","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"mailto","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Relative URLs stay as they are:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let generator = HtmlGenerator(safeMode: true)","let html = generator.generate(doc: MarkdownParser.standard.parse(\"[x](javascript:alert(1))\"))"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/StringGenerator","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/TerminalGenerator","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" replace control and bidirectional formatting characters with U+FFFD, so the text of a document cannot inject escape sequences into a terminal.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Choose-rendering-options-for-attributed-strings","level":3,"text":"Choose rendering options for attributed strings","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"By default, images referred to by Markdown may be loaded from any location: the system’s HTML renderer loads any file that an image URL points to (also files outside of ","type":"text"},{"code":"imageBaseUrl","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", reached via ","type":"text"},{"code":"../","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or absolute paths), and ","type":"text"},{"code":"generateAsync","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" additionally fetches ","type":"text"},{"code":"http(s)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" images and style sheets. Only the path extension of an image is checked by default (see below).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For untrusted Markdown, use the preset ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/RenderingOptions-swift.struct/untrusted","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (safe mode, and no local and no remote images):","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let generator = AttributedStringGenerator(renderingOptions: .untrusted)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Its counterpart ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/RenderingOptions-swift.struct/trusted","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" restricts nothing; it is the same as the default options, ","type":"text"},{"code":"RenderingOptions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". To allow some images, restrict image loading with the options ","type":"text"},{"code":"localImages","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"remoteImages","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead. Each is an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/ImageAccess","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Value","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Meaning","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".none","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"never load","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".any","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"no restriction in terms of URL path","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".within(url)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"local images: only image files inside this directory, symbolic links resolved; remote images: only URLs with the same scheme, host and port as ","type":"text"},{"code":"url","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and a path below the path of ","type":"text"},{"code":"url","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table"},{"code":["let imageDirectory = URL(fileURLWithPath: \"/path/to/images\", isDirectory: true)","let options = AttributedStringGenerator.RenderingOptions(","                baseUrl: imageDirectory,","                localImages: .within(imageDirectory),","                remoteImages: .within(URL(string: \"https://example.com/images/\")!),","                textSizeMultiplier: 1.2)","let generator = AttributedStringGenerator(renderingOptions: options)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Independently of the location checks, every image that is checked must also have one of the path extensions in ","type":"text"},{"code":"imageExtensions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (default: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/RenderingOptions-swift.struct/defaultImageExtensions","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": png, jpg, jpeg, gif, tif, tiff, bmp, ico, heic, heif, webp), whether its location was permitted by ","type":"text"},{"code":".any","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":".within","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; this keeps non-image files from being loaded via an image URL. A custom set replaces the default, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" stands for URLs without extension. This check always applies to the images of the Markdown text, also if ","type":"text"},{"code":"localImages","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"remoteImages","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are both ","type":"text"},{"code":".any","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Know-what-the-restrictions-do-not-cover","level":3,"text":"Know what the restrictions do not cover","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Images in raw HTML are not checked, and the restrictions apply to the images of the Markdown text only: raw HTML in the Markdown can still refer to images, style sheets and other resources. Set ","type":"text"},{"code":"safeMode: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the options to also omit raw HTML and to limit links to the schemes ","type":"text"},{"code":"http","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"https","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"mailto","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; it is independent of the image options and ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by default.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Images that are not allowed are replaced by their alternative text. Relative image paths are resolved against ","type":"text"},{"code":"imageBaseUrl","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or, if that is not set, against ","type":"text"},{"code":"baseUrl","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; the access options never influence this resolution, they only check the resolved URL (relative paths are rejected if there is no base).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"With ","type":"text"},{"code":"remoteImages: .none","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and Markdown without raw HTML, ","type":"text"},{"code":"generateAsync","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does not access the network. Remote images are never loaded by the synchronous methods.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The restrictions are enforced while generating the HTML; they do not cover resources the application itself refers to (e.g. via ","type":"text"},{"code":"customStyle","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), redirects of web servers, or files that change between the check and loading.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Without restrictions, do not use ","type":"text"},{"code":"generateAsync","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with untrusted Markdown, as it then loads remote resources (images, style sheets) that the HTML refers to.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Important","style":"important","type":"aside"},{"anchor":"Draw-diagrams-safely","level":3,"text":"Draw diagrams safely","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Mermaid diagrams are drawn in a web view that cannot access the network or local files and has no connection to the rest of the application, and Mermaid runs with ","type":"text"},{"code":"securityLevel: 'strict'","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DrawingMermaidDiagrams","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Limit-nesting","level":3,"text":"Limit nesting","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Deeply nested input does not overflow the stack: the nesting depth is limited to 24 (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DocumentParser/maxContainerDepth","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/InlineParser/maxNestingDepth","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"); deeper markup stays text.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"View-untrusted-Markdown-in-SwiftUI","level":3,"text":"View untrusted Markdown in SwiftUI","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownText","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" uses ","type":"text"},{"code":"RenderingOptions.trusted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by default. Pass ","type":"text"},{"code":"renderingOptions: .untrusted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to its initializers if the document does not come from a trusted source:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["MarkdownText(string: text, renderingOptions: .untrusted)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit":{"abstract":[{"text":"Parse, process and display text in Markdown format.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"MarkdownKit","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator":{"abstract":[{"code":"AttributedStringGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" provides functionality for converting Markdown blocks into","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSAttributedString","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" objects that are used in macOS and iOS for displaying rich text.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The implementation is extensible allowing subclasses of ","type":"text"},{"code":"AttributedStringGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"override how individual Markdown structures are converted into attributed strings.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AttributedStringGenerator"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AttributedStringGenerator"}],"role":"symbol","title":"AttributedStringGenerator","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/attributedstringgenerator"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/ImageAccess":{"abstract":[{"text":"Describes which images of one kind (stored locally or loaded from the web) may be loaded.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ImageAccess"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/ImageAccess","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ImageAccess"}],"role":"symbol","title":"AttributedStringGenerator.ImageAccess","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/attributedstringgenerator/imageaccess"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/RenderingOptions-swift.struct/defaultImageExtensions":{"abstract":[{"text":"The default for ","type":"text"},{"code":"imageExtensions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"defaultImageExtensions"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh","text":"Set"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/RenderingOptions-swift.struct/defaultImageExtensions","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"defaultImageExtensions","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/attributedstringgenerator/renderingoptions-swift.struct/defaultimageextensions"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/RenderingOptions-swift.struct/trusted":{"abstract":[{"text":"Options for rendering Markdown which comes from a trusted source (for example documents","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written by the author of the application, or files of the user). It is the counterpart","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of ","type":"text"},{"code":"untrusted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and nothing is restricted: raw HTML in the Markdown is passed on, links","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can use any scheme, and images stored in the local file system as well as images from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the web may be loaded (remote images are only loaded by the asynchronous methods; the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"synchronous ones never load them). As always, the path extension of every image has to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be one of ","type":"text"},{"code":"imageExtensions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". All other options have their default value.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"trusted"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit25AttributedStringGeneratorC","text":"AttributedStringGenerator"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit25AttributedStringGeneratorC16RenderingOptionsV","text":"RenderingOptions"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/RenderingOptions-swift.struct/trusted","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"trusted","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/attributedstringgenerator/renderingoptions-swift.struct/trusted"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/RenderingOptions-swift.struct/untrusted":{"abstract":[{"text":"Options for rendering Markdown which does not come from a trusted source (for example","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"text written by other users, or by a language model). Raw HTML in the Markdown is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"omitted, links are limited to the schemes ","type":"text"},{"code":"http","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"https","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"mailto","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (and relative","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"URLs), and no image of the Markdown text is loaded, neither a local one nor one from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the web: images are replaced by their alternative text. Everything else has the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default value (see the initializer), e.g. ","type":"text"},{"code":"timeout","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"defaultTimeout","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"untrusted"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit25AttributedStringGeneratorC","text":"AttributedStringGenerator"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit25AttributedStringGeneratorC16RenderingOptionsV","text":"RenderingOptions"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/RenderingOptions-swift.struct/untrusted","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"untrusted","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/attributedstringgenerator/renderingoptions-swift.struct/untrusted"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DocumentParser/maxContainerDepth":{"abstract":[{"text":"The maximal nesting depth of containers (block quotes and list items).","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maxContainerDepth"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DocumentParser/maxContainerDepth","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"maxContainerDepth","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/documentparser/maxcontainerdepth"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DrawingMermaidDiagrams":{"abstract":[{"text":"Show fenced code blocks with the language ","type":"text"},{"code":"mermaid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as diagrams in attributed strings.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DrawingMermaidDiagrams","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Drawing Mermaid Diagrams","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/drawingmermaiddiagrams"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/GeneratingOutput":{"abstract":[{"text":"Convert a parsed Markdown document into HTML, attributed strings, plain text or text for ANSI terminals.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/GeneratingOutput","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Generating Output","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/generatingoutput"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/HtmlGenerator":{"abstract":[{"code":"HtmlGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" provides functionality for converting Markdown blocks into HTML. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"implementation is extensible allowing subclasses of ","type":"text"},{"code":"HtmlGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to override how","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"individual Markdown structures are converted into HTML.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HtmlGenerator"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/HtmlGenerator","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"HtmlGenerator"}],"role":"symbol","title":"HtmlGenerator","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/htmlgenerator"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/InlineParser/maxNestingDepth":{"abstract":[{"text":"The maximal nesting depth of inline markup (links, images, emphasis).","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maxNestingDepth"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/InlineParser/maxNestingDepth","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"maxNestingDepth","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/inlineparser/maxnestingdepth"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownText":{"abstract":[{"text":"A SwiftUI view that displays a Markdown document as formatted text. The view converts the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"document into an attributed string with an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", using different","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"generators for light and dark mode, and shows the result in a read-only text view whose text","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can be selected. The view scrolls vertically.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MarkdownText"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownText","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MarkdownText"}],"role":"symbol","title":"MarkdownText","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/markdowntext"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/StringGenerator":{"abstract":[{"code":"StringGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" provides functionality for converting Markdown blocks into formatted","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plain text strings with word wrapping and indentation support. The implementation is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"extensible allowing subclasses of ","type":"text"},{"code":"StringGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to override how individual Markdown","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"structures are converted into strings.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"StringGenerator"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/StringGenerator","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"StringGenerator"}],"role":"symbol","title":"StringGenerator","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/stringgenerator"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/TerminalGenerator":{"abstract":[{"code":"TerminalGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" provides functionality for converting Markdown blocks into text for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ANSI-compliant terminals, with word wrapping, indentation, and styled text. The result is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"marked up with ANSI escape sequences. The implementation is extensible allowing subclasses","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of ","type":"text"},{"code":"TerminalGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to override how individual Markdown structures are converted into","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"styled text.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TerminalGenerator"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/TerminalGenerator","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TerminalGenerator"}],"role":"symbol","title":"TerminalGenerator","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/terminalgenerator"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/UsingTheCommandLineTools":{"abstract":[{"text":"Convert Markdown files from the terminal and preview the text generators.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/UsingTheCommandLineTools","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Using the Command-Line Tools","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/usingthecommandlinetools"}},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Generating-output","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/GeneratingOutput","doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/UsingTheCommandLineTools"],"title":"Generating output"}],"variants":[{"paths":["/documentation/markdownkit/renderinguntrustedmarkdown"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}]}